[{:db/id 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-87c89c45-3edb-5cd5-88f1-a3ee2b4d8003"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-87c89c45-3edb-5cd5-88f1-a3ee2b4d8003" :question/id #uuid "87c89c45-3edb-5cd5-88f1-a3ee2b4d8003" :question/math-academy-id "q-35640" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices $({a}_{ij})$  with real entries, such that  ${a}_{11}+{a}_{22}$ is rational.  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$T$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of matrices by a real number) because $\\text{____}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is \n\n*$T$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of matrices by a real number) because **multiplication by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\n For example, the identity matrix \n\n$$\nI=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nlies in $T$, but\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\cdot I=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\notin T\n$$\n\nbecause $\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}$ is not a rational number.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- The zero matrix belongs to $T.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices with real entries is commutative, in general.    $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices with real entries is associative, in general.    $\\,✓$\n\n- Given any $A\\in T,$  the additive inverse matrix $-A=(-1)\\cdot A$ is also in  $T,$ and   $A+(-A)=O.$  $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-047ee837-df71-5e5c-bcee-335a715a816d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-047ee837-df71-5e5c-bcee-335a715a816d" :answer-field/id #uuid "047ee837-df71-5e5c-bcee-335a715a816d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f89006ab-36a7-5769-850c-8ee5d58a71d1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-97a1f3dc-dc3c-53f9-b457-30bca1c9f80b" "answer-6c610fab-a6ec-5612-9143-78410e0c0685" "answer-d008fb5f-392d-5a1e-8353-f48e8e0933c4" "answer-f89006ab-36a7-5769-850c-8ee5d58a71d1" "answer-952805ec-db79-5003-ab44-c608da27648b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97a1f3dc-dc3c-53f9-b457-30bca1c9f80b" :answer/id #uuid "97a1f3dc-dc3c-53f9-b457-30bca1c9f80b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$T$ does not contain the zero matrix $O$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c610fab-a6ec-5612-9143-78410e0c0685" :answer/id #uuid "6c610fab-a6ec-5612-9143-78410e0c0685" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of matrices in $T$ is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d008fb5f-392d-5a1e-8353-f48e8e0933c4" :answer/id #uuid "d008fb5f-392d-5a1e-8353-f48e8e0933c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of matrices in $T$ is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f89006ab-36a7-5769-850c-8ee5d58a71d1" :answer/id #uuid "f89006ab-36a7-5769-850c-8ee5d58a71d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplication by a scalar is not closed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-952805ec-db79-5003-ab44-c608da27648b" :answer/id #uuid "952805ec-db79-5003-ab44-c608da27648b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "there exists a matrix $A\\in T$ such that $A+B\\ne O$ for any $B\\in T.$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2d091317-3092-5633-8a6e-4652d2fd3389"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2d091317-3092-5633-8a6e-4652d2fd3389" :question/id #uuid "2d091317-3092-5633-8a6e-4652d2fd3389" :question/math-academy-id "q-106941" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $u$ and $v$ are vectors such that $x+u=x+v$ for some $x\\in V,$ then $u=v.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+u & =x+v &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+u)+(-x) & =(x+v)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+u & =x+v &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+u)+(-x) & =(x+v)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A1}\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-29e9d841-9401-5444-9a3a-2b082af4b7ae"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-29e9d841-9401-5444-9a3a-2b082af4b7ae" :answer-field/id #uuid "29e9d841-9401-5444-9a3a-2b082af4b7ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-506393e5-9110-55a4-ad28-86b41af5f7b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-506393e5-9110-55a4-ad28-86b41af5f7b7" "answer-f44ae4d3-7509-5333-9443-9a689afb980d" "answer-94a3dcc7-829d-5b5b-838b-243af61af1c7" "answer-3f2283d3-68c5-5fca-946c-408c6fb2b791" "answer-b61ef8ae-4ec6-5626-8687-752c08d8c0f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-506393e5-9110-55a4-ad28-86b41af5f7b7" :answer/id #uuid "506393e5-9110-55a4-ad28-86b41af5f7b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f44ae4d3-7509-5333-9443-9a689afb980d" :answer/id #uuid "f44ae4d3-7509-5333-9443-9a689afb980d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94a3dcc7-829d-5b5b-838b-243af61af1c7" :answer/id #uuid "94a3dcc7-829d-5b5b-838b-243af61af1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f2283d3-68c5-5fca-946c-408c6fb2b791" :answer/id #uuid "3f2283d3-68c5-5fca-946c-408c6fb2b791" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b61ef8ae-4ec6-5626-8687-752c08d8c0f4" :answer/id #uuid "b61ef8ae-4ec6-5626-8687-752c08d8c0f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-ea1bef1c-e09c-5c2e-9d55-d2d0c3cb38cd" :activity/id #uuid "ea1bef1c-e09c-5c2e-9d55-d2d0c3cb38cd" :activity/title "Defining Abstract Vector Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049064 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-467837ce-9aea-5bd2-99a0-3354bf395104" "step-f72bd130-061d-5d95-9582-1d1554fa5cad" "step-f97b0645-0a69-5367-a434-1456880e7389" "step-bbaac633-758e-54a8-bb41-3769e90b4fe8" "step-0e561cf1-bbce-5b45-99d8-35b7ea403736"] :activity/first-step "step-467837ce-9aea-5bd2-99a0-3354bf395104" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-467837ce-9aea-5bd2-99a0-3354bf395104" :step/id #uuid "467837ce-9aea-5bd2-99a0-3354bf395104" :step/content "question-87c89c45-3edb-5cd5-88f1-a3ee2b4d8003" :step/next "step-f72bd130-061d-5d95-9582-1d1554fa5cad" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f72bd130-061d-5d95-9582-1d1554fa5cad" :step/id #uuid "f72bd130-061d-5d95-9582-1d1554fa5cad" :step/content 17592186419007 :step/next "step-f97b0645-0a69-5367-a434-1456880e7389" :db/ensure [:step/validat